    NOTICE OF INTENT TO USE MATERIAL DESIGNATED AS CONFIDENTIAL

       Pursuant to Section L of the Protective Order issued in this proceeding, the Regents of New

Mexico State University (“NMSU”) hereby provide notice that NMSU intends to use, in its pre-

filed testimony and exhibits and at the hearing in this matter, material designated by El Paso

Electric Company ("EPE") as confidential, contained in the following:

      EPE Response to Staff's Data Request No. 1-2, Attachment 13 CONFIDENTIAL

      EPE Response to Staff's Data Request No. 1-2, Attachment 06 CONFIDENTIAL

      EPE Response to NMDOJ's Data Request No. 01-05, Attachment 01 CONFIDENTIAL

       MATERIAL

      EPE Response to NMDOJ's Data Request No. 01-05, Attachment 02 CONFIDENTIAL

       MATERIAL

       The CONFIDENTIAL Direct Testimony of Michael P. Gorman on behalf of NMSU

includes material designated by EPE as confidential on pages 22, 25 and 27, and in

CONFIDENTIAL Exhibit MPG-21. These pages are marked CONFIDENTIAL as required by

Section E of the Protective Order. A Confidential version of Mr. Gorman's testimony, with no

redactions, will be filed electronically in the PRCe360 docket system as confidential and served

by email only to EPE, the Hearing Examiners, and to those persons that have signed

Confidentiality Agreements. A Public version of Mr. Gorman's testimony, with redactions of
 material designated by EPE as confidential, will be filed electronically in the PRCe360 docket

system and served on those persons on the service list.

                                     Respectfully submitted on October 23, 2026,

